      "hints": [
        "Use the ideal gas equation $pV = nRT$ to determine the amount of gas $n$ in moles.",
        "Ensure the volume is converted from $\\text{cm}^3$ to $\\text{m}^3$ using $1\\,\\text{cm}^3 = 10^{-6}\\,\\text{m}^3$ before calculating."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Recall the ideal gas equation: $pV = nRT$, rearranged as $n = \\frac{pV}{RT}$.",
        "Substitute initial state values: $p = 3.0 \\times 10^5\\,\\text{Pa}$, $V = 210 \\times 10^{-6}\\,\\text{m}^3$, $R = 8.31\\,\\text{J}\\,\\text{K}^{-1}\\,\\text{mol}^{-1}$, $T = 270\\,\\text{K}$.",
        "Calculate $n = \\frac{3.0 \\times 10^5 \\times 210 \\times 10^{-6}}{8.31 \\times 270} = \\frac{63}{2243.7} = 0.0281\\,\\text{mol} \\approx 0.028\\,\\text{mol}$."
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "deterministic_checks": [],
        "full_marks_if_all_deterministic_checks_pass": false,
        "ai_rubric": [
          {
            "criterion_id": "9702_s19_43_q02_a_i_mp01",
            "observable": "States or uses the ideal gas equation $pV = nRT$."
          },
